## 🧹 Data Preprocessing

Several preprocessing steps were performed before model training.

### 1. Remove ID

The `ID` column was removed because it is an identifier and does not represent meaningful passenger information.

### 2. Train/Test Split

The dataset was divided into:

```text
80% Training
20% Testing
```

A stratified split was used to preserve the target distribution.

### 3. Missing Values

Numerical missing values were handled using:

```text
Median Imputation
```

Categorical missing values were handled using:

```text
Most Frequent Value
```

### 4. Categorical Encoding

Categorical features were converted into numerical features using:

```text
One-Hot Encoding
```

### 5. Feature Scaling

Numerical features were standardized using:

```text
StandardScaler
```

### 6. Pipeline

The preprocessing steps were implemented inside a **Scikit-learn Pipeline** and **ColumnTransformer**.

This helps prevent data leakage because preprocessing is fitted only on the training data during model training and cross-validation.

